From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wayland-workspace: Take the scroll wheel over the buttons

The workspace switcher changes the workspace with the scroll wheel. Its
handler is on the pager widget, which on Wayland is a grid of toggle
buttons. The grid has no window, and a button does not ask for scroll
events, so GDK gave a scroll over a button to the panel's window, and the
handler never ran: the wheel did nothing over the Wayland switcher.

Ask for scroll events on each button, as the Wayland window list does for
its own, so that the event goes up from the button through the grid.
---
 applets/wncklet/wayland-workspace.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/applets/wncklet/wayland-workspace.c b/applets/wncklet/wayland-workspace.c
index 4d16027c..c8bd268c 100644
--- a/applets/wncklet/wayland-workspace.c
+++ b/applets/wncklet/wayland-workspace.c
@@ -297,6 +297,9 @@ rebuild_ui (WaylandWorkspaceData *data)
 		g_free (free_name);
 
 		gtk_widget_set_name (button, "wnck-pager-button");
+		/* A button takes no scroll events of its own, and the applet's
+		 * handler for the wheel is on the grid, which has no window. */
+		gtk_widget_add_events (button, GDK_SCROLL_MASK);
 		g_object_set_data (G_OBJECT (button), "ws-index", GINT_TO_POINTER (i));
 
 		/* Set active state */
